  "body": "See https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28150 for background.\n\nThis is simply an editorial change related to one of the spec’s document-conformance requirements for authors (and not at all to requirements for UAs). This change adds a non-normative note to clarify to authors that if a `select` element does not have a `sizes` attribute with a value greater than `1`, then the element must have a `placeholder` attribute.\n\nFor context on why it’s worded the way it is, see https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28150\n\nI raised this originally because, after I added code to the HTML Checker (aka validator) to enforce this requirement, somebody reported a bug against the checker, and their bug report indicated that they were confused about why the checker was claiming they needed to add a `placeholder` attribute. And the reason was because they didn’t have a `sizes` attribute with a value greater than `1` (but they could not tell that from reading the spec, because the spec does not clearly state that).\n",
